we've seen tons of lawsuits being filed  with headline grabbing numbers being  filed for  say billions of dollars the billion  dollar lawsuit from dominion or  billions of dollars being sought from  facebook and google but here's a secret  that only lawyers know  that number is largely bs the thing is  the plaintiff can put whatever  allegations they want  into the complaint and the number that  they seek at the very end  of the complaint the prayer for relief  is going to have  a large number often if you're launching  a lawsuit that has as much of a pr  component as it does an actual legal  basis then you're gonna want to grab  some headlines and a lot of these  lawsuits have  done that it doesn't mean that they're  entitled to that amount of money doesn't  mean that they're going to be awarded  that amount of money from the judge or  the jury  it just means that a plaintiff's lawyer  wants to cover their bases  and they want to make sure that they're  not hamstrung by seeking a small amount  upfront so they will put  basically any number that they want at  the end of the complaint so just  remember that next time you see a  lawsuit that is seeking billions of  dollars from someone else that number is  largely made up
 

